1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 30=

4
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,479
Does Your Majesty think

5
00:00:54,119 --> 00:00:55,359
reopening the cottage case

6
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,759
and punishing Zhang Heng
and Zhang Yuying

7
00:00:58,679 --> 00:01:00,439
was enough to answer to the realm?

8
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:02,960
You knew all along.

9
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,520
You knew they

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,280
embezzled funds at court

11
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:07,520
and killed people in the harem.

12
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:09,320
You simply decided

13
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,640
those commoners' lives

14
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:12,680
weren't worth turning on them for.

15
00:01:13,439 --> 00:01:14,799
Only when you had no choice

16
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:16,920
did you finally answer to the realm.

17
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:18,840
You reopened the Guizhen Cottage case,

18
00:01:19,439 --> 00:01:20,439
announced it to the realm,

19
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:22,000
and declared justice served.

20
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,519
At that moment, did you really think

21
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,599
you were a benevolent ruler?

22
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,000
No.

23
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:31,640
You're just a hypocrite

24
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:33,040
who let those crimes happen,

25
00:01:33,799 --> 00:01:34,840
then years later

26
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:38,719
used them to make yourself look good.

27
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,319
You...

28
00:01:52,079 --> 00:01:53,079
Chen Shouhe,

29
00:01:53,799 --> 00:01:54,640
my husband,

30
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,000
with your tacit consent,

31
00:01:57,599 --> 00:01:59,760
your beloved consort
had him tortured to death.

32
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:01,680
His blood

33
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,439
splashed onto the dragon's eye.

34
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:06,359
Yet you praised it as the perfect touch

35
00:02:06,599 --> 00:02:08,560
and admired it year after year.

36
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:10,319
You even said

37
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,959
staying here beside Roujia

38
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,400
was a blessing for him.

39
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:23,199
You never cared about a commoner's life.

40
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:24,719
All you care about

41
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,800
is your realm,

42
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:28,680
your power,

43
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:30,520
your facade as a benevolent ruler.

44
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:33,879
So you...

45
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:34,759
So...

46
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:35,560
So you...

47
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,319
You've been...

48
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:39,159
deceiving me all along.

49
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,560
Your Majesty,

50
00:03:02,879 --> 00:03:04,960
what do you think is inside

51
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,360
the herbal sachet beneath your pillow?

52
00:03:13,479 --> 00:03:15,319
The grass woven into the screen

53
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,240
is called Same-Root Grass.

54
00:03:17,919 --> 00:03:19,159
When one stalk dies,

55
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,080
the other

56
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,719
becomes a noose that

57
00:03:24,439 --> 00:03:25,599
slowly tightens

58
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,560
until its enemy dies.

59
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:31,680
You've slept on that herbal sachet
for hundreds of nights.

60
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,800
The poison has seeped into your bones.

61
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,759
And the incense I just burned

62
00:03:38,439 --> 00:03:39,400
was the catalyst.

63
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,000
Your Majesty.

64
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:45,479
You're completely helpless now.

65
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,439
Guards!

66
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,960
Guards!

67
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,639
Stop shouting.

68
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:59,120
Everyone in this hall

69
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:00,879
answers to me.

70
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:02,800
Your Majesty.

71
00:04:03,439 --> 00:04:04,919
You sowed these seeds yourself.

72
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,280
Now you reap what you sowed.

73
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,400
All of this

74
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:11,120
is exactly what you deserve.

75
00:04:17,479 --> 00:04:18,000
Su.

76
00:04:18,599 --> 00:04:19,120
Su.

77
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,599
Did you really

78
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:22,759
never

79
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:24,839
love me,

80
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,319
not even a little?

81
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,639
Every day I've lived

82
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,240
was spent waiting for this moment.

83
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:40,639
As for the love you asked about,

84
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,560
I could never

85
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,639
have loved you.

86
00:04:59,079 --> 00:05:00,759
Su Cao!

87
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,199
Su Cao!

88
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,600
(If...)

89
00:05:14,879 --> 00:05:16,279
(there is another life,)

90
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:18,360
(I...)

91
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,759
(will live as)

92
00:05:21,439 --> 00:05:23,279
(an ordinary woman,)

93
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,399
(and marry a man I love.)

94
00:05:28,439 --> 00:05:29,000
(Never)

95
00:05:29,279 --> 00:05:30,000
(again...)

96
00:05:31,639 --> 00:05:32,959
(will I enter)

97
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,319
(Your Majesty's...)

98
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:35,560
(high-walled)

99
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,639
(palace.)

100
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:39,360
Roujia.

101
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,880
(Pure Heart, Serene Mind)

102
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:14,920
His Majesty is bedridden.

103
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,120
From now on, it's up to you.

104
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,800
You're leaving?

105
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,079
From this day forward,

106
00:06:22,399 --> 00:06:24,079
there will be no Noble Consort Hui.

107
00:06:35,079 --> 00:06:36,560
(Once this palace job is done
and I get paid,)

108
00:06:37,519 --> 00:06:39,040
(I'll buy you a fur collar)

109
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:40,519
(to keep your throat warm.)

110
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,079
(Wanniang.)

111
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,480
(Wait for me.)

112
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,560
I could never figure out

113
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,720
who in this palace

114
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,560
gave Shouhe

115
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,519
that fur collar.

116
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,480
So it was you.

117
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:14,319
Fur...

118
00:07:15,199 --> 00:07:15,920
What did you say?

119
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:16,639
Fur...

120
00:07:17,639 --> 00:07:18,399
collar...

121
00:07:22,519 --> 00:07:22,920
Here.

122
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:39,800
Thank you.

123
00:07:43,519 --> 00:07:43,959
Consort Yu.

124
00:07:44,319 --> 00:07:45,160
Take good care of Zhao.

125
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,120
Don't worry.

126
00:07:48,879 --> 00:07:49,519
I'm leaving.

127
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,959
How is His Majesty?

128
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,439
(Grand Halls and Deep Chambers)
No word.

129
00:08:07,439 --> 00:08:08,959
What are we supposed to do?

130
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:10,040
I'm worried sick.

131
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,000
His Majesty

132
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,800
will be all right, won't he?

133
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,000
His Majesty is gravely ill.

134
00:08:17,199 --> 00:08:18,040
He can no longer speak

135
00:08:18,279 --> 00:08:19,160
or support himself.

136
00:08:19,759 --> 00:08:21,120
He can no longer govern in person.

137
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,759
His Majesty may not recover.

138
00:08:27,759 --> 00:08:29,240
A realm can't go a day without a ruler.

139
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,639
We ask Prince Ning

140
00:08:30,839 --> 00:08:32,040
to govern in His Majesty's stead

141
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:33,480
and keep the realm stable.

142
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:50,600
Wanniang!

143
00:08:50,799 --> 00:08:51,279
Wanniang!

144
00:08:51,799 --> 00:08:52,759
News from the capital!

145
00:08:53,039 --> 00:08:53,759
His Majesty has passed away.

146
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:54,919
Prince Ning took the throne.

147
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:55,960
He's lowering taxes

148
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:56,720
and reducing forced labor.

149
00:08:56,879 --> 00:08:58,120
He'll rule with benevolence.

150
00:09:03,919 --> 00:09:05,120
(Shouhe.)

151
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,720
(Did you see?)

152
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,760
(The End)

153
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:30,547
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

154
00:09:30,681 --> 00:09:34,294
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

155
00:09:34,529 --> 00:09:37,128
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

156
00:09:37,165 --> 00:09:39,445
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

157
00:09:39,492 --> 00:09:43,321
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

158
00:09:43,723 --> 00:09:47,076
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

159
00:09:48,003 --> 00:09:51,516
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

160
00:09:52,016 --> 00:09:54,583
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

161
00:09:54,709 --> 00:09:56,742
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

162
00:09:56,809 --> 00:10:00,586
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

163
00:10:00,936 --> 00:10:05,269
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

164
00:10:05,492 --> 00:10:08,999
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

165
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:12,033
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

166
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:17,714
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

167
00:10:17,754 --> 00:10:20,768
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

168
00:10:20,809 --> 00:10:26,817
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

169
00:10:27,484 --> 00:10:34,439
♪The past has faded away♪

170
00:10:34,439 --> 00:10:37,471
♪The past has faded away♪
